  "comment": "B1 Round 23 — quarantine-on-fork algorithm vectors. Spec authz/event-auth-state-resolution.md §6 + §7: when concurrent forks land on the same (kind, state_key) cell, the reducer MUST NOT pick a winner automatically (no LWW timestamp tiebreak). Instead all non-winners (or all heads, depending on lattice bottom mode) are quarantined and require admin escalation. cas-register cells with bottom=reject yield Bottom Conflict; or-set cells expose the union (no conflict); ordered-log appends both branches. The vectors below cover concurrent forks across the cas-register lattice (admin escalation REQUIRED) and confirm that the reducer never auto-resolves.",
  "encoder": {
    "spec": "authz/event-auth-state-resolution.md §6 + §7",
    "algorithm": "On concurrent fork at the same (kind, state_key): if lattice has bottom=reject → all participating ops quarantined, cell remains Bottom; if lattice=or-set → both ops merged into the union; if lattice=ordered-log → both ops admitted, ordered by HLC."
  },
